{"term":"rejoice","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a54e7f3451d57d685e","definition":"To be very happy, be delighted, exult; to feel joy.","example":"Obscurity, indeed, is painful to the mind as well as to the eye ; but to bring light from obscurity, by whatever labour, must needs to be delightful and rejoicing.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["blithen","delight","rapture"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["rejoiceful","rejoiceless","rejoicement","rejoicer","rejoicingly","unrejoiced","unrejoicing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:68d2ae6042aa2d5925","definition":"To have (someone) as a lover or spouse; to enjoy sexually.","example":"ye that are a knyghte wyueles that ye wyl not loue some mayden or gentylwoman /[…]/ but hit is noysed that ye loue quene Gueneuer / and that she hath ordeyned by enchauntement that ye shal neuer loue none other / but her / ne none other damoysel ne lady shall reioyse you","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["rejoiceful","rejoiceless","rejoicement","rejoicer","rejoicingly","unrejoiced","unrejoicing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a757b6b0aeca3d843c","definition":"To make happy, exhilarate.","example":"Were he [Cain] alive, it would rejoice his soul to see what mischief it had made.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["elate","happify","beatify","enrapture","begladden","blissen","bright","cheer","fetch","cheer up","cherish","content","delight","elate","elevate","enbliss","exhilarate","fain","gay","gladden","gladden someone's heart","gratify","happify","happy","hearten","jollify","laetificate","light up","make someone's day","perk up","please","raise someone's spirits","rejoice","turn the frown upside down","upcheer","warm someone's heart","warm the cockles of someone's heart"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["rejoiceful","rejoiceless","rejoicement","rejoicer","rejoicingly","unrejoiced","unrejoicing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7f9f985782d002357c","definition":"To enjoy.","example":"c. 1449–1455, Reginald Peacock, Represser of over-much weeting [blaming] of the Clergie\nhis brother Constans next aftir him rejoiced the same west-parti.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["rejoiceful","rejoiceless","rejoicement","rejoicer","rejoicingly","unrejoiced","unrejoicing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rejoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɹɪˈd͡ʒɔɪs/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b8/En-us-rejoice.ogg/En-us-rejoice.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["rejoiceful","rejoiceless","rejoicement","rejoicer","rejoicingly","unrejoiced","unrejoicing"]}